        </div>
        <h4>Zig-Zag Rows</h4>
        <p>Image and text alternate sides row to row. Slower to scan than a grid, better for telling a sequence of points.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.4rem; background:var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.4rem;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.4rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="height:1.8rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Tabs</h4>
        <p>One panel visible at a time behind a row of switches. Keeps a busy page short at the cost of hiding content.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="gap:3px;">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="flex:1;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="flex:1;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="flex:1;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>List / Table</h4>
        <p>Rows of structured data. Pricing comparisons, changelogs, specs: anything better scanned than read.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row" style="justify-content:center;">
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.4rem;height:1.8rem; opacity:.5;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.8rem;height:2.2rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-box" style="width:1.4rem;height:1.8rem; opacity:.5;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Carousel</h4>
        <p>One item centered and emphasized, neighbors peeking at the edges. Good for testimonials, risky for anything important.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem; opacity:.6;">The shape should fit the content, not the other way around.</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissContentTypesModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal modal-large" id="footerTypesModal" aria-labelledby="footerTypesTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="footerTypesTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Footers, Four Ways</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeFooterTypesModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <div class="type-gallery">
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center;">
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div><div class="type-bar" style="width:1.2rem;"></div></div>
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:2.5rem;"></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Minimal</h4>
        <p>A few links and a copyright line. Right for small sites with nothing else that needs saying.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--row">
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="flex:1;"><div class="type-bar" style="background:var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar"></div><div class="type-bar"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="flex:1;"><div class="type-bar" style="background:var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar"></div><div class="type-bar"></div></div>
          <div class="type-mock--col" style="flex:1;"><div class="type-bar" style="background:var(--pink);"></div><div class="type-bar"></div><div class="type-bar"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Mega Footer</h4>
        <p>A full sitemap in columns. Common on large sites where the footer doubles as secondary navigation and SEO.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; text-align:center;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:2.2rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-box" style="flex:1; height:0.9rem;"></div><div class="type-box" style="width:1.2rem;height:0.9rem; background:var(--pink);"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>Newsletter Footer</h4>
        <p>An email field and a button, front and center. The footer as one last chance to capture the visitor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="type-example">
        <div class="type-mock type-mock--col" style="align-items:center; text-align:center;">
          <div class="type-bar" style="width:2rem;"></div>
          <div class="type-mock--row"><div class="type-box" style="width:1.6rem;height:1rem;"></div><div class="type-box" style="width:1.6rem;height:1rem;"></div></div>
        </div>
        <h4>App-Download Footer</h4>
        <p>Store badges instead of links. For products where the real destination is a mobile app, not more web pages.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span class="mono" style="font-size:0.75rem; opacity:.6;">Same last impression, different jobs.</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissFooterTypesModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal" id="contrastCheckerModal" aria-labelledby="contrastCheckerTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="contrastCheckerTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Contrast Checker</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeContrastCheckerModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <p>Real WCAG math, calculated in your browser as you type. No values are sent anywhere.</p>
    <div class="contrast-inputs">
      <label class="contrast-field">
        <span>Text color</span>
        <span class="contrast-field__row">
          <input type="color" id="ccFgPicker" value="#22182B" aria-label="Text color picker" />
          <input type="text" id="ccFgHex" value="#22182B" class="contrast-field__hex mono" maxlength="7" aria-label="Text color hex value" />
        </span>
      </label>
      <label class="contrast-field">
        <span>Background color</span>
        <span class="contrast-field__row">
          <input type="color" id="ccBgPicker" value="#FFF9F2" aria-label="Background color picker" />
          <input type="text" id="ccBgHex" value="#FFF9F2" class="contrast-field__hex mono" maxlength="7" aria-label="Background color hex value" />
        </span>
      </label>
    </div>

    <div class="contrast-preview" id="ccPreview">
      <p style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; margin:0;">The quick fox jumps.</p>
      <p style="margin:0.3rem 0 0;">Body text at a normal reading size.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="contrast-result">
      <div class="contrast-result__ratio" id="ccRatio">21.00 : 1</div>
      <div class="contrast-badges" id="ccBadges">
        <span class="contrast-badge" data-key="aaNormal">AA Normal Text</span>
        <span class="contrast-badge" data-key="aaLarge">AA Large Text</span>
        <span class="contrast-badge" data-key="aaaNormal">AAA Normal Text</span>
        <span class="contrast-badge" data-key="aaaLarge">AAA Large Text</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mono" style="font-size:0.72rem; opacity:.6; margin-top:0.75rem;">Normal text needs 4.5:1 (AA) or 7:1 (AAA). Large text (18px+, or 14px+ bold) and UI borders need 3:1 (AA) or 4.5:1 (AAA).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span></span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissContrastCheckerModal">Got it</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal" id="contrastGameModal" aria-labelledby="contrastGameTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="contrastGameTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">Guess the Contrast</h2>
    <button type="button" class="icon-btn" id="closeContrastGameModal" aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__body">
    <p>Would this pass WCAG AA for normal text (4.5:1)? Guess before you check the math.</p>
    <span class="quiz-score" id="cgScore" aria-live="polite">Score: 0 / 0</span>
    <div class="contrast-preview" id="cgPreview" style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <p style="font-size:1.2rem; font-weight:700; margin:0;">Sample Text</p>
      <p style="margin:0.3rem 0 0;">This is what body copy looks like in this pairing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cg-guess-row" id="cgGuessRow">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="cgGuessPass">Passes AA</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" id="cgGuessFail">Fails AA</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cg-result" id="cgResult" hidden>
      <p id="cgResultText" style="margin:0;"></p>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" id="cgNext" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">Next pair</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="modal__footer">
    <span></span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="dismissContrastGameModal">Done</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog class="modal modal-large" id="styleGuideModal" aria-labelledby="styleGuideTitle">
  <div class="modal__header">
    <h2 id="styleGuideTitle" style="font-size: 1.25rem;">This Page's Style Guide</h2>
